 "guide": {
  "overview": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Zenematics' pure mage: every school on one character. Summons and fireball staffs early, Scorching Ray with weakness spells in the mid game, and Shadow Clones casting Forbidden Sun at the end."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Recreated level by level from his video guide, How to Mage (LoreRim 5.0). Perks are placed at the first level the rules allow, in the order the video takes them."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "The free spells Zen picks with his first tier perks are shown on screen rather than named, so those picks are left open. Every spell he names is in, at the level he gets it."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "level:1": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Start with Guilds, College of Winterhold. Get College Robes from Mirabelle, skip the tour and loot the Hall of the Elements. Do every lesson with Tolfdir and the other tutors: it's XP you need before going out. Healing and Conjure Spirit Wolf are lying around the College."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "level:2": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Tolfdir's extra lesson teaches Waterbreathing, then a dive with Arniel Gane. Keep going through the tutors."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "level:4": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Faralda's lesson gives Fireball, your damage until everything else comes online. Then Windhelm: wait out a night nearby to start Blood on the Ice for the Necromancer's Amulet. Wuunferth the Unliving in the Palace of the Kings sells Eldritch Blast now, and Witch Bolt and Cloudkill later."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "level:5": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Take the fireball staff from the Altar of Magnus, and the second one by the Thalmor Embassy. Pray at the Magna-Ge's altar near Bleak Falls at 7 pm and follow the Magna-Ge from here: staff charges refill on their own."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "level:6": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Mentor's Ring at the Ritual Stone. Outside Falkreath's south-east gate, Flying Fred's journal marks the paraglider; a forge can turn it into a levitation gem."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "level:7": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Every attribute goes to Magicka: health and stamina come from spells. Skills: Conjuration, Alteration and Restoration to 50 first, then Destruction and Enchanting."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "level:8": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Power-level on the undead werewolf packs: one near the College, one north-west of Stonehills, one by Darkshade. Use the ground, keep your distance, and wait with staffs drawn to recharge them."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "level:13": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "The level-12 set is done: Adept Conjuration with Bound Armor, Empowered Conjuration and Cognitive Flexibility for a second summon, Adept Destruction with Flame Sphere and Scorching Ray, Adept Restoration with Resist Poison on Self, Alteration up to Apprentice with Oakflesh, Ocato's Recital and Featherfall, and the first Enchanting perks. Buy Ice Armor, Featherwalking and Visions of Opportunity."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "level:14": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Darkshade: kill Ulik the troll and skin him. In the Arcanaeum, read the Armorer's Encyclopedia without taking it (Smithing 10) for Craftsmanship, buy Cloth Padding and forge Elemental Padding."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "level:16": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Aim for Enchanting 75 to make expert staffs. Clear Saarthal and push the College quests to Mzulft. Flame Sphere does the work in tight caves."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "level:18": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Mzulft: Elemental Susceptibility is in a book by the bed on the scaffolding. In the Arch-Mage's Quarters, take the heart stones while he's out, and Race Against Time."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "level:20": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Ragnvald for Otar's mask, Shriekwind Bastion's safe for Denstagmer's Ring. Agent of Mara and Sirenroot add more magic resistance. Dragon priests: Race Against Time, both weakness spells, then Scorching Ray."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "level:25": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "The Slow Time shout is in Deepwood Redoubt, reached through the Civil War's Jagged Crown."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "level:30": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Make two Cloudkill staffs at a Staff Enchanter. They melt dragons, more so after a weakness spell."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "level:32": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Labyrinthian. Loot the wisp wrappings from the wispmothers. Morokei: wait on the bridge until his health dips about 10%, then Slow Time, the weakness spells and Scorching Ray. Learn Conjure Ghostly Frost Lich afterwards; no more Conjuration perks from here."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "level:34": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Finish the College: Ancano's Gloves, the Arch-Mage Robes and Boots. Most of the game can be done in this set."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "level:40": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Endgame starts. Septimus Signus' quest gives the Oghma Infinium: six skills +5 and 3 perk points. In the Forgotten Vale, the Sapphire Paragon opens the inner sanctum: Arcane Cross needs the wisp wrappings, diamonds and black soul gems. Urag's quest Shalidor's Insight gives Shalidor's Mirror, the best ward."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "level:50": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Master Illusion for Shadow Clone on Self, with Master of Shadows, Shadow Shaping and Shadows of Conflict for more clones. Each clone casts what you hold when you summon it."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "level:55": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Endgame gear. Forbidden Sun only casts from the left hand, so put it on a staff too and the clones copy both."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "level:57": {
   "type": "doc",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "The finished build: clones casting Forbidden Sun to strip fire resistance, Sotha's Maelstrom against magic resistance, Mimic's Cloak to fire spells back out, Godform for magicka and Spirit of the Sun to heal."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 }
}